<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:11:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Deadly Russian attacks damage two bridges in Kyiv, mayor says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says</link><description>
Russian attacks on Kyiv killed three people and damaged two bridges in the Ukrainian capital, city authorities said on Friday. The fresh wave of missile and drone attacks came after Russian President Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" retaliation after Ukraine this week damaged the Crimea bridge. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f85d74-e4ab-11f1-8758-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T015437Z-618531473-RC2DROAHQAD6-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f85d74-e4ab-11f1-8758-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T015437Z-618531473-RC2DROAHQAD6-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c85c9ea-e4ab-11f1-a114-d3a799165f5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:32:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f85d74-e4ab-11f1-8758-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T015437Z-618531473-RC2DROAHQAD6-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Thomas Peter, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Czechs protest en masse against 'concentration of power in one hand' and growing control over media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over-media</link><description>
As large demonstrations in the Czech Republic challenge Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's plans to change the funding model of public broadcasters, Mikuláš Minář, Chair of the Million Moments for Democracy movement, joins François Picard from Prague for Spotlight, warning that his country risks following Hungary and Slovakia in democratic backsliding. "We are really afraid that the Czech Republic is following the Orbánian Hungarian way, (Fico's) Slovakian way," he says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8a83266-e4a7-11f1-b6fc-0f49ce47132d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:02:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU and UK set to sign deals on trade, energy, youth mobility at Brussels summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit</link><description>
The UK and the EU are poised to agree new deals on trade, energy and youth mobility at a summit in Brussels on Friday, as part of UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's bid to reset ties with the bloc. Burnham – who has said he hopes to see Britain rejoin the EU in his lifetime – argues the deals will help fix some of the damage Brexit inflicted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/203b3d22-e486-11f1-9e19-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/c90a23b59a6d01ee8ae6acbb2cad20e56147ea25.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/203b3d22-e486-11f1-9e19-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/c90a23b59a6d01ee8ae6acbb2cad20e56147ea25.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">215366b2-e486-11f1-8392-c54bec5a97cd</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:00:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/203b3d22-e486-11f1-9e19-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/c90a23b59a6d01ee8ae6acbb2cad20e56147ea25.jpg">© Carlos Jasso, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>PM Sanchez admits 'mistakes' in key debate ahead of Spain's election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s%C3%A1nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election</link><description>
Spain's Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez acknowledged shortcomings in his government on Thursday as he faced conservative rival Alberto Nunez Feijoo in the campaign's only televised debate. The November 29 election could leave the far-right Vox party in a position to enter government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47a90c40-e47c-11f1-823f-bb1d3788691b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:49:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg">© Jaime Reina, Josep Lago, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian strikes on Kyiv kill one, damage Dutch and Austrian embassies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies</link><description>
A wave of daytime Russian strikes on Kyiv on Thursday killed one person and damaged a historic cathedral as well as the embassies of Austria and the Netherlands. Loud explosions erupted across the Ukraine capital throughout the day as the leaders of Russia, China and the United States held a historic meeting in China that put Russia's President Vladimir Putin in international spotlight. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58fdce58-e45f-11f1-99b5-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-203931-204127-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58fdce58-e45f-11f1-99b5-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-203931-204127-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5eb9e890-e45f-11f1-ab0f-8dbb507a1f19</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:25:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kushner says Trump 'open' to extend NATO mutual defense-type clause to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine</link><description>
US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday that President Donald Trump was open to extending to Ukraine a security guarantee similar to NATO's mutual defense clause, but stressed that Washington has to protect its interests too. The comments came as German Chancellor Friedrich Merz qualified the summit between the presidents of the United States, Russia and China as a "photo op". FRANCE 24's international affairs commentator Douglas Herbert explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25b84e6c-e444-11f1-a13d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T175030Z-1149809636-RC24ROAX76LX-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25b84e6c-e444-11f1-a13d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T175030Z-1149809636-RC24ROAX76LX-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e2b59d8-e452-11f1-b9df-1b5e5e3e7684</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:41:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron urges Ukraine's allies to 'reopen the question' of NATO membership</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday called for Ukraine's allies to speed up the delivery of urgently needed air defence systems and urged them to "reopen the question" of Ukraine's NATO membership after talks in Berlin aimed at reaffirming European support for Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4326a9aa-e456-11f1-8321-2f542a93f4a9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:32:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg">© Hannah McKay, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Three of a kind? Xi hosts Trump and Putin as Ukraine war grinds on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on</link><description>
Gang of three or glorified photo op? Xi Jinping hosting Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Already, our Monday panel rejected attempts to paint the three-way meeting as a new Yalta, as in the 1945 sit-down on the Black Sea that defined the post-war security architecture of Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cf1dff8-e44b-11f1-81ed-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T112415Z-149699658-RC2ZQOAH0BR6-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cf1dff8-e44b-11f1-81ed-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T112415Z-149699658-RC2ZQOAH0BR6-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c65e57fc-e44a-11f1-91b0-ff7f8e5d3944</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:39:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Behind the UK's use of AI in asylum applications</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications</link><description>
The UK is increasingly turning to artificial intelligence to manage its immigration system, from analysing migrants’ phones to processing asylum applications. But what happens when AI gets involved in deciding how an asylum seeker's story is understood? Stella Elgersma, journalist at InfoMigrants, explains how the UK Home Office is testing AI tools to process asylum applications, including a system that generates summaries of asylum interviews. With errors, limited human oversight and concerns over transparency, could AI put asylum seekers’ lives at risk?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e36442a-e428-11f1-a386-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-143639-144049-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e36442a-e428-11f1-a386-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-143639-144049-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33d74b0e-e428-11f1-8380-35699edb96b7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:07:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin</link><description>
The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf9490a-e41f-11f1-8a6b-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-140128-140711-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf9490a-e41f-11f1-8a6b-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-140128-140711-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3513e08-e41f-11f1-ae06-0db31b1ab018</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:04:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine's European allies meet in Berlin in show of support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support</link><description>
Ukraine’s main European allies are meeting in Berlin on Thursday as a show of support for Kyiv, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also attending. The gathering, which brings together the leaders of Germany, France, Britain, Poland and Italy as well as NATO chief Mark Rutte, takes place as Trump and Putin meet in China, fuelling fears in Europe that decisions on the war could be made without its input. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Germany has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8491ffc-e400-11f1-9722-0f0809d6071d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:43:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump</link><description>
Denmark's parliament on Thursday ratified a security deal involving Greenland and the United States. The vote comes months after the US, Denmark and Greenland ​signed the ‌agreement to end a standoff with the Trump administration over the Arctic island's future. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/337a8fc4-e3fe-11f1-82a1-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266587574802.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/337a8fc4-e3fe-11f1-82a1-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266587574802.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2324459e-e3fd-11f1-81b8-d3313f191154</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:08:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/337a8fc4-e3fe-11f1-82a1-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266587574802.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin to rally support for Kyiv after Trump-Putin-Xi talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks</link><description>
Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin on Thursday to shore up support for Kyiv just hours after Russia's Vladimir Putin took part in a historic trilateral meeting with US President Donald Trump and China's Xi Jinping. The "Coalition of the Willing" summit comes as Europe is hoping to secure a seat at the table of any future peace talks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92fca864-e41d-11f1-980c-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26323457805562.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92fca864-e41d-11f1-980c-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26323457805562.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8c83dce-e3c4-11f1-a73b-116921ae379c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:55:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92fca864-e41d-11f1-980c-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26323457805562.jpg">© Bernd von Jutrczenka, DPA via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding</link><description>
Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5df44426-e3bc-11f1-be92-6d9f3ae22326</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:00:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg">© Yasin Akgul, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Crimea bridge strike: Fact-checking fake videos of damage after Ukraine's attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack</link><description>
Ukraine has struck the Kerch Bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, but not all the dramatic footage circulating online is real. Multiple AI-generated videos falsely show the bridge collapsed with extensive damage. Some even used branding resembling a Ukrainian news agency to appear credible. While the bridge was indeed struck and damaged, the viral videos were fabricated using AI, as Vedika Bahl explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5b1bea-e39a-11f1-83bd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/kerch.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5b1bea-e39a-11f1-83bd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/kerch.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ed05ade-e39a-11f1-8df1-35772d82a0de</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:51:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Why Ukraine keeps trying to bring down Russia's bridge to Crimea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea</link><description>
A Ukrainian drone and missile strike on Monday night brought down a stretch of the bridge linking the annexed Crimean Peninsula to Russia, potentially crippling a route long used by Moscow to move men and materiel into Crimea and the southern front. Here’s why Kyiv keeps testing its strength against an infrastructure project that has become synonymous with Russian President Vladimir Putin’s 2014 seizure of the peninsula.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f055bd98-e373-11f1-a1da-21f28020077c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:17:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg">© Security Service of Ukraine handout via Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>War in Ukraine: Is France in direct conflict with Russia?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia</link><description>
An investigation published by the French public radio channel RFI on November 17 revealed that a confidential mission by the French army known as "Volia" has been used for months to conceal the presence of French personnel in Ukraine. Russia was prompt to accuse France of direct involvement in the conflict. Is this true?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8cecea6e-e36a-11f1-b640-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/French-troops-Ukraine-10.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8cecea6e-e36a-11f1-b640-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/French-troops-Ukraine-10.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1857d58-e36a-11f1-b037-f9b6f7051788</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:57:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia’s new low-cost munitions pose a fresh threat to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine</link><description>
Dan-T, Filin and Geran-5 might not mean anything to you, but in Ukraine, everyone is talking about these munitions. These new Russian weapons are small, fast and cheap – and a major threat, as they were specially designed to get around Ukrainian anti-aircraft defences and strike deep within the country.
