Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is asserting that the United States has asked him about a straight-up swap: Russia gets the Donbas and the rest of Ukraine gets NATO membership – a guarantee against Moscow later having a second go and annexing the entire country. Whether or not the offer is real, serious or either side would accept it is another matter. We ask if the talk of partition signals some kind of turning point in a nearly five-year war that's at a brutal stalemate.
